{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773437311,"nonce":"MjhJtAv1yOu7xs7idiW+I8YoNkg=","title":"mandible issue: missing subcommands — new, label, list, open","message":"The mandible issue CLI only exposes close, comment, show. All issue operations should be available without reaching for git-bug directly.\n\nMissing subcommands:\n- `mandible issue new -t \u003ctitle\u003e -m \u003cbody\u003e` — create a new issue (wraps git-bug bug new --non-interactive)\n- `mandible issue label add \u003cid\u003e \u003clabel\u003e` — add a label (wraps git-bug bug label new)\n- `mandible issue label rm \u003cid\u003e \u003clabel\u003e` — remove a label (wraps git-bug bug label rm)\n- `mandible issue list [--status open|closed|all]` — list issues (wraps git-bug bug --status)\n- `mandible issue open \u003cid\u003e` — reopen a closed issue (wraps git-bug bug status open)\n\nThe goal is that agents working in repos that have mandible available never need to know git-bug syntax directly — mandible issue is the single interface.","files":null}]}